01:53:13,840 --> 01:53:14,520
That's the handbrake.

2138
01:53:16,360 --> 01:53:18,420
Oh, I took it from within the car.

2139
01:53:18,620 --> 01:53:18,900
Sick.

2140
01:53:20,070 --> 01:53:22,410
Keep cash safe by storing it in your stash at home.

2141
01:53:22,610 --> 01:53:22,750
Alright.

2142
01:53:28,250 --> 01:53:29,030
Wha-?

2143
01:53:34,950 --> 01:53:35,350
Sorry!

2144
01:53:36,030 --> 01:53:37,150
You were in the way, man.

2145
01:53:39,770 --> 01:53:40,830
Okay, whatever you say.

2146
01:53:44,840 --> 01:53:46,360
Man, I'm in love with this already.

2147
01:53:49,020 --> 01:53:49,500
What's that?

2148
01:53:50,060 --> 01:53:51,640
Hey, this is Joey from Coastal Auto Care.

2149
01:53:51,880 --> 01:53:53,400
Cal mentioned your car might need some work.

2150
01:53:53,580 --> 01:53:53,940
Let me know.

2151
01:53:54,040 --> 01:53:54,540
Here's my spot.

2152
01:53:56,100 --> 01:53:57,000
When I get a minute, sure.

2153
01:54:02,200 --> 01:54:03,060
Cool, see you then.

2154
01:54:03,160 --> 01:54:07,580
Wait, can I actually... Don't text and drive.

2155
01:54:09,360 --> 01:54:10,200
It's a bad idea.

2156
01:54:12,760 --> 01:54:13,740
Oh, police.

2157
01:54:14,320 --> 01:54:15,100
What's happening here?

2158
01:54:15,180 --> 01:54:15,980
Excuse me, officer.

2159
01:54:18,540 --> 01:54:19,560
Don't try to cry.

2160
01:54:35,530 --> 01:54:36,730
Good looking out, officer.

2161
01:54:36,990 --> 01:54:38,150
Keep the neighborhood safe.

2162
01:54:45,380 --> 01:54:47,220
Man, I am just taking in these visuals.

2163
01:54:47,520 --> 01:54:48,280
I'm drinking it up.

2164
01:54:48,660 --> 01:54:48,840
Oh, shit.

2165
01:54:52,220 --> 01:54:53,480
North Toll 1A.

2166
01:54:53,560 --> 01:54:55,900
Why is there an animal on that?

2167
01:54:58,520 --> 01:54:59,940
Wait, should I go to the gun store first?

2168
01:55:00,080 --> 01:55:00,360
Wait a minute.

2169
01:55:01,020 --> 01:55:02,040
Let me see if I can make a sick turn.

2170
01:55:07,440 --> 01:55:08,500
There's a gun store over here.

2171
01:55:13,560 --> 01:55:14,640
You guys don't mind, do you?

2172
01:55:15,300 --> 01:55:15,720
Yepsy!

2173
01:55:18,740 --> 01:55:19,560
Let's have a look.

2174
01:55:21,020 --> 01:55:21,940
Oh, man.

2175
01:55:22,100 --> 01:55:24,120
Dude, these environments, I can't get enough.

2176
01:55:25,380 --> 01:55:25,920
It's part.

2177
01:55:38,300 --> 01:55:38,940
Ammu-nation.

2178
01:55:50,540 --> 01:55:51,500
Approach and do.

2179
01:55:53,708 --> 01:55:56,475
Oh shit, Jason D.

2180
01:55:57,008 --> 01:56:00,008
Didn't recognize you for a sec. These eyes.

2181
01:56:03,360 --> 01:56:04,760
Oh?

2182
01:56:05,008 --> 01:56:07,008
What's up, Andrew, how ya doing?

2183
01:56:07,008 --> 01:56:27,008
I'm good soldier, I'm good. You said you needed something?

2184
01:56:37,420 --> 01:56:41,440
Wait a minute, operator?

2185
01:56:41,700 --> 01:56:43,380
Does that mean I was Special Forces or something?

2186
01:56:43,520 --> 01:56:44,500
I don't know what that term means.

2187
01:56:46,008 --> 01:56:47,492
So... got some good rifles.

2188
01:56:47,558 --> 01:56:50,758
The Hawk & Little there, the Mediator, hell of a carbine.

2189
01:56:51,008 --> 01:56:54,525
They ran that in the sandbox. All these babies shoot true, though.

2190
01:56:55,008 --> 01:56:59,075
Or.. if you want a platform that just does what it says on the tin,

2191
01:56:59,258 --> 01:57:01,108
you could go with the Moreland 850 there.

2192
01:57:01,342 --> 01:57:03,908
Pump action, thing's got stoppin' power.

2193
01:57:04,508 --> 01:57:06,442
Yeah... yeah, maybe those could work.

2194
01:57:07,410 --> 01:57:09,170
Didn't I already get one of those, though?

2195
01:57:09,630 --> 01:57:10,650
In the last mission?

2196
01:57:15,325 --> 01:57:20,258
I know, 'cause I went through the trainin', but you know that.

2197
01:57:21,720 --> 01:57:23,260
I mean, I already have a gun, don't I?

2198
01:57:25,158 --> 01:57:26,658
Take a minute, at ease...

2199
01:57:28,240 --> 01:57:29,880
Let's go for a shotgun, then.

2200
01:57:33,440 --> 01:57:35,320
Fortune and son, Moreland 850.

2201
01:57:36,860 --> 01:57:37,820
Oh, I saw it off.

2202
01:57:39,660 --> 01:57:40,720
Ooh, I like the look of that.

2203
01:57:44,180 --> 01:57:44,560
Yeah.

2204
01:57:49,560 --> 01:57:49,940
Ooh.

2205
01:57:54,260 --> 01:58:00,380
Why are some of these yellow stickers... Wait a minute, I just said that out loud.

2206
01:58:00,520 --> 01:58:01,120
Yellow sticker.

2207
01:58:01,740 --> 01:58:04,860
I think that's actually like a term they use in the US for something.

2208
01:58:05,160 --> 01:58:06,940
Maybe these are the ones he has discounted.

2209
01:58:08,580 --> 01:58:12,500
I'll take a... a flashlight attachment.

2210
01:58:13,580 --> 01:58:14,800
Bright hour tactical.

2211
01:58:16,480 --> 01:58:17,080
Yeah.

2212
01:58:17,860 --> 01:58:19,360
Oh, you get to choose.

2213
01:58:20,880 --> 01:58:22,800
Handling is a little worse like this.

2214
01:58:23,980 --> 01:58:26,320
But is the light better?

2215
01:58:27,280 --> 01:58:28,400
Let's go with that one.

2216
01:58:29,040 --> 01:58:29,840
Smart choice.

2217
01:58:30,320 --> 01:58:31,400
Get it and send it.

2218
01:58:32,440 --> 01:58:32,920
Okay.

2219
01:58:35,080 --> 01:58:35,800
Thanks, brother.

2220
01:58:36,760 --> 01:58:37,240
Cosmetics.

2221
01:58:40,000 --> 01:58:41,140
Oh, that's expensive.

2222
01:58:41,420 --> 01:58:42,420
We gotta go make some money.

2223
01:58:48,270 --> 01:58:48,950
Thanks, brother.

2224
01:58:50,690 --> 01:58:54,350
Purchase, modify, and manage your weapons at Ammunations across Leonida.

2225
01:58:55,430 --> 01:58:56,450
Chuck's Tackle and Shot.

2226
01:58:56,530 --> 01:58:57,390
That's a cool name for a story.

2227
01:58:58,750 --> 01:59:01,130
Openly carrying weapons can be dangerous in Leonida.

2228
01:59:01,490 --> 01:59:03,730
Manage them at any weapon locker and your vehicle's trunk.

2229
01:59:04,230 --> 01:59:04,990
Oh, shit!

2230
01:59:05,290 --> 01:59:10,010
So finally, if you just run around like a madman, it's not gonna go well for you.

2231
01:59:10,650 --> 01:59:14,450
You can carry an axis up to two sidearms and two long arms.

2232
01:59:14,630 --> 01:59:14,790
Okay.

2233
01:59:15,720 --> 01:59:17,340
Dude, look at this strap, too!

2234
01:59:18,920 --> 01:59:19,840
I love that.

2235
01:59:21,160 --> 01:59:23,280
It will expand their stock as you purchase more weapons.

2236
01:59:23,600 --> 01:59:23,840
Nice.

2237
01:59:25,380 --> 01:59:29,220
Well, you can't have a shotgun without also having some nice glasses, right?

2238
01:59:30,740 --> 01:59:31,820
Let's see what we got here.

2239
01:59:32,200 --> 01:59:33,000
Fishing shades.

2240
01:59:36,000 --> 01:59:39,920
You know, all I need with these glasses now is a pickup truck, and I'm a true American.

2241
01:59:42,840 --> 01:59:45,500
I guess I'll take... No, it's too edgy.

2242
01:59:46,300 --> 01:59:47,300
I can't do that.

2243
01:59:48,560 --> 01:59:49,680
Buy some ammo.

2244
01:59:50,000 --> 01:59:53,780
I still can't believe you can just walk into a shop in the US and buy a fucking gun.

2245
01:59:55,400 --> 01:59:56,620
That's crazy, bro.

2246
01:59:57,440 --> 01:59:58,360
Scorpio nipper.

2247
01:59:59,420 --> 01:59:59,940
Alright.

2248
02:00:01,560 --> 02:00:02,720
It's a girl's gun.

2249
02:00:03,160 --> 02:00:04,080
Not for me.

2250
02:00:05,940 --> 02:00:06,920
Fishing lines!

2251
02:00:09,520 --> 02:00:10,240
There's fishing.

2252
02:00:11,620 --> 02:00:13,700
Attracts medium saltwater fish species.

2253
02:00:14,280 --> 02:00:15,360
Oh my god.

2254
02:00:16,400 --> 02:00:17,620
We need to go fishing.

2255
02:00:19,940 --> 02:00:20,540
Parachute.

2256
02:00:20,720 --> 02:00:21,140
Nice.

2257
02:00:21,960 --> 02:00:22,400
Okay.

2258
02:00:23,160 --> 02:00:23,860
What about this?

2259
02:00:24,120 --> 02:00:25,480
Can I get some more paint for my house?

2260
02:00:28,140 --> 02:00:29,040
Hey, Andrew.

2261
02:00:30,020 --> 02:00:31,020
Ah, we're good.

2262
02:00:32,520 --> 02:00:33,760
Is that a real skull?

2263
02:00:34,000 --> 02:00:34,720
Or head?

2264
02:00:35,680 --> 02:00:36,980
Of a crocodile?

2265
02:00:37,820 --> 02:00:38,420
Headwear.

2266
02:00:39,710 --> 02:00:40,930
I guess I'm a cap guy.

2267
02:00:43,170 --> 02:00:43,790
It's alright.

2268
02:00:46,010 --> 02:00:46,930
Let me see this.

2269
02:00:47,430 --> 02:00:48,170
Manage weapons.

2270
02:00:50,810 --> 02:00:52,670
So this is everything I own, I guess.

2271
02:00:53,550 --> 02:00:56,670
Pistol, shotgun, melee.

2272
02:00:58,890 --> 02:00:59,910
Oh, so wait a minute.

2273
02:01:00,210 --> 02:01:03,210
Maybe you need to buy things to actually own them.

2274
02:01:03,950 --> 02:01:05,350
So they're gonna be in this locker.

2275
02:01:05,610 --> 02:01:07,250
Like the shotgun I got from that mission.

2276
02:01:07,610 --> 02:01:09,490
I think it was just like what I had in that mission.

2277
02:01:11,210 --> 02:01:13,850
But these are the ones I own, and they can be stored here.

2278
02:01:15,450 --> 02:01:15,770
Cool.

2279
02:01:16,650 --> 02:01:20,470
But, I mean, should I really be walking around with a shotgun on my back?

2280
02:01:21,990 --> 02:01:25,790
I mean, I get it's the US and all, but even that is a little crazy, isn't it?

2281
02:01:27,850 --> 02:01:28,170
Okay.

2282
02:01:29,970 --> 02:01:30,810
That was kind of nuts.

2283
02:01:31,310 --> 02:01:31,630
Oh!

2284
02:01:35,560 --> 02:01:37,100
Uh, sorry?

2285
02:01:37,600 --> 02:01:38,760
I got a shotgun.

2286
02:01:38,980 --> 02:01:39,640
You see that, right?

2287
02:01:40,100 --> 02:01:41,160
This is the States, brother.

2288
02:01:42,600 --> 02:01:43,100
Oh!

2289
02:01:45,360 --> 02:01:46,180
The fuck?

2290
02:01:47,160 --> 02:01:49,160
I was just trying to warn them off!

2291
02:01:49,525 --> 02:01:50,975
You shoulda stayed in the swamp, fellas..

2292
02:01:51,860 --> 02:01:52,560
Fuck yeah.

2293
02:01:54,940 --> 02:01:55,440
Alright.

2294
02:01:56,060 --> 02:01:57,760
Let me take a picture of you guys.

2295
02:01:59,540 --> 02:02:00,280
Look at that.

2296
02:02:00,380 --> 02:02:01,620
Look at how dumb you look right now.

2297
02:02:01,800 --> 02:02:03,880
This is you after trying to mess with me.

2298
02:02:04,700 --> 02:02:05,220
Dumbass.

2299
02:02:07,600 --> 02:02:08,920
Your buddy right there.

2300
02:02:09,900 --> 02:02:11,020
Crime scene photos.

2301
02:02:12,520 --> 02:02:13,040
Beautiful.

2302
02:02:14,160 --> 02:02:15,240
You can put a filter on.

2303
02:02:17,440 --> 02:02:17,960
Sweet.

2304
02:02:24,360 --> 02:02:25,560
Killed some thugs.

2305
02:02:25,920 --> 02:02:26,960
Might delete later.

2306
02:02:28,960 --> 02:02:30,080
Light off.

2307
02:02:30,440 --> 02:02:31,360
Yeah, keep the light off.

2308
02:02:32,340 --> 02:02:34,340
What's with the little things in the bottom there?

2309
02:02:35,820 --> 02:02:37,020
How do I take the picture?

2310
02:02:38,300 --> 02:02:39,200
There we go.

2311
02:02:39,880 --> 02:02:40,400
Lovely.

2312
02:02:41,120 --> 02:02:41,440
Okay!

2313
02:02:42,180 --> 02:02:43,400
Don't mess with Jason!

2314
02:02:44,960 --> 02:02:46,200
I just had a lisp there.

2315
02:02:47,200 --> 02:02:47,960
Got a knife?

2316
02:02:48,180 --> 02:02:48,640
Thank you.

2317
02:02:49,380 --> 02:02:50,220
What do you got on you?

2318
02:02:51,480 --> 02:02:52,260
Mm-hmm.

2319
02:02:52,750 --> 02:02:53,570
Oh, a hat.

2320
02:02:53,690 --> 02:02:54,610
Would you look at that.

2321
02:02:55,810 --> 02:02:56,210
Sweet.

2322
02:02:56,370 --> 02:02:56,870
Thank you, fellas.

2323
02:02:57,530 --> 02:02:59,490
Oh, and is that a car for me as well?

2324
02:02:59,990 --> 02:03:01,550
Hold on, we got a revolver.

2325
02:03:03,710 --> 02:03:04,790
I'll be taking that.

2326
02:03:05,090 --> 02:03:05,390
Thank you.

2327
02:03:06,130 --> 02:03:07,090
Wait, I can open the trunk.

2328
02:03:08,890 --> 02:03:09,810
Still long arms.

2329
02:03:12,930 --> 02:03:13,830
Actually, you know what?

2330
02:03:15,310 --> 02:03:16,470
Can I grab that again?

2331
02:03:16,970 --> 02:03:17,730
Take long arms.

2332
02:03:19,290 --> 02:03:20,290
I don't want this car.

2333
02:03:20,570 --> 02:03:21,210
It's too American.

2334
02:03:21,970 --> 02:03:24,970
I was joking before with the pickup, but I don't actually want to drive in that.

2335
02:03:25,670 --> 02:03:26,810
What are you doing, Jason?

2336
02:03:27,950 --> 02:03:28,370
Throw?

2337
02:03:29,090 --> 02:03:30,150
You can throw the knife?

2338
02:03:34,330 --> 02:03:34,810
Damn!

2339
02:03:35,610 --> 02:03:36,190
Sick throw.

2340
02:03:37,870 --> 02:03:38,350
Alright.

2341
02:03:38,850 --> 02:03:39,590
Good talk.

2342
02:03:40,990 --> 02:03:42,230
I got places to be.

2343
02:03:45,240 --> 02:03:51,240
I mean, I was trying to, you know, scare them off by aiming it at them, but then they freaking pulled out guns in response.

2344
02:03:53,360 --> 02:03:54,800
I guess people here are pretty aggressive.

2345
02:03:54,980 --> 02:03:55,420
Oh, sorry!

2346
02:03:55,620 --> 02:03:55,860
Sorry!

2347
02:03:57,840 --> 02:03:58,200
Whoa!

2348
02:03:58,560 --> 02:03:59,060
Excuse me!

2349
02:04:01,575 --> 02:04:05,942
Hey, Donne, just a heads up, the kingfishers jumped me, man.

2350
02:04:06,442 --> 02:04:07,375
Oh shit.

2351
02:04:12,360 --> 02:04:14,780
Sounds like you got a little sloppy there, hoss.

2352
02:04:15,080 --> 02:04:17,240
Keep your head on the swivel, okay?

2353
02:04:17,580 --> 02:04:18,860
Stay in the game.

2354
02:04:19,140 --> 02:04:21,580
Ain't nobody jumping my white ass, no siree.

2355
02:04:21,700 --> 02:04:22,640
Yeah, sure, Dom.

2356
02:04:23,640 --> 02:04:24,340
Stay safe.

2357
02:04:24,820 --> 02:04:25,560
Always, man.

2358
02:04:25,900 --> 02:04:26,320
You too.

2359
02:04:29,560 --> 02:04:30,440
Okay, Donnie.

2360
02:04:31,360 --> 02:04:32,860
Maybe he can also be a nice friend.

2361
02:04:33,300 --> 02:04:36,040
He does seem a little crazy, though, and a little bit of a drug addict.

2362
02:04:37,320 --> 02:04:40,860
Like him, you know, snorting that shit while flying the plane?

2363
02:04:41,720 --> 02:04:42,780
It's kind of a bad sign.

2364
02:04:42,780 --> 02:04:43,960
You don't want that guy as a pilot.

2365
02:04:50,630 --> 02:04:51,190
Oh.

2366
02:04:51,190 --> 02:04:53,710
Some guy just came from off-roading.

2367
02:04:54,990 --> 02:04:58,350
Man, I can't get over how good this game looks, man.

2368
02:04:59,450 --> 02:05:00,450
It's incredible.

2369
02:05:01,690 --> 02:05:02,390
Come in here.

2370
02:05:05,310 --> 02:05:07,590
Your actions will affect your criminal profile.

2371
02:05:07,850 --> 02:05:09,270
It may have a lasting impact.

2372
02:05:09,930 --> 02:05:11,630
Hold right to check your current status.

2373
02:05:12,990 --> 02:05:14,770
Okay, so I'm orange right now.

2374
02:05:17,050 --> 02:05:18,350
I want to become green.

2375
02:05:18,650 --> 02:05:19,530
Like a Kerbal.

2376
02:05:20,730 --> 02:05:21,530
And go to space.

2377
02:05:21,850 --> 02:05:21,930
Oh!

2378
02:05:23,170 --> 02:05:24,090
There you are!

2379
02:05:26,490 --> 02:05:27,230
What's up, brother?

2380
02:05:28,725 --> 02:05:33,625
Don't do that! You went stealth mode on me, bro. I'm still jumpy.

2381
02:05:34,525 --> 02:05:36,192
Brian said something about picking up a payment?

2382
02:05:36,358 --> 02:05:38,358
Oh yeah, that's right.

2383
02:05:38,458 --> 02:05:42,708
I knew there was something. Okay, let's take my truck.

2384
02:05:44,080 --> 02:05:46,120
Okay, but... what about my car, though?

2385
02:05:50,342 --> 02:05:53,208
Man, I gotta get in better shape.

2386
02:05:54,140 --> 02:05:56,280
Dude, I thought we were gonna go fishing, at least.

2387
02:05:56,520 --> 02:05:57,740
Just a little bit, but alright.

2388
02:05:58,840 --> 02:05:59,600
Wait, open?

2389
02:06:00,980 --> 02:06:01,760
That's crazy!

2390
02:06:03,870 --> 02:06:04,270
Aha!

2391
02:06:05,510 --> 02:06:05,910
Sweet.

2392
02:06:06,410 --> 02:06:08,130
You get to see stats by doing that?

2393
02:06:08,370 --> 02:06:08,650
Nice.

2394
02:06:09,670 --> 02:06:11,130
Should I be stowing this in the back?

2395
02:06:12,110 --> 02:06:13,870
Along with this fish and tackle or whatever?

2396
02:06:14,770 --> 02:06:15,350
Or not.

2397
02:06:15,770 --> 02:06:15,990
Okay.

2398
02:06:16,770 --> 02:06:17,990
And we can only do that with my car.

2399
02:06:19,070 --> 02:06:20,070
So you want me to drive?

2400
02:06:20,210 --> 02:06:20,770
Okay, got it.

2401
02:06:20,870 --> 02:06:22,410
Sorry, I'm a little bit out of it.

2402
02:06:23,370 --> 02:06:25,310
I was reading a crazy story at home just now.

2403
02:06:25,890 --> 02:06:26,770
About the Germans.

2404
02:06:27,790 --> 02:06:28,530
Sauerkraut and shit.

2405
02:06:29,670 --> 02:06:29,990
Alright.

2406
