It's funny how they kind of nail the shit people write online these days, but you can still tell that it's, like, written by somebody who may not actually be in that circle, you know?

4804
04:30:17,400 --> 04:30:18,300
All caught up.

4805
04:30:18,460 --> 04:30:18,800
Okay.

4806
04:30:20,020 --> 04:30:20,480
Awesome.

4807
04:30:20,620 --> 04:30:21,100
No reminders.

4808
04:30:21,900 --> 04:30:22,560
That's cool.

4809
04:30:23,020 --> 04:30:23,680
What's this?

4810
04:30:23,880 --> 04:30:25,040
Oh, that's the scrolling thing.

4811
04:30:25,140 --> 04:30:25,620
Let's see the news.

4812
04:30:28,120 --> 04:30:32,200
Vice City Police Department Officer Guilty of Really Gross Negligence.

4813
04:30:32,880 --> 04:30:33,520
Alright.

4814
04:30:34,240 --> 04:30:35,500
By Jalen Taylor.

4815
04:30:36,520 --> 04:30:43,200
A VCPD policeman has admitted that he lost control of his squad car because he was watching porn site booty bang on his cell.

4816
04:30:44,160 --> 04:30:54,060
Officer Hank Driscoll was pursuing a suspected carjacker in downtown, but then mounted the sidewalk and flipped his car, narrowly escaping the vehicle before it caught fire and exploded.

4817
04:30:54,940 --> 04:30:56,680
Dude, these cops are...

4818
04:30:57,430 --> 04:30:58,510
Fake cops, man.

4819
04:30:59,330 --> 04:31:04,790
Driscoll explained that he found watching pornography very calming during car chases, but that the video had frozen.

4820
04:31:05,190 --> 04:31:06,310
It was so frustrating.

4821
04:31:06,650 --> 04:31:10,330
The dude had walked in on his hot stepmom having a shower, and then nothing.

4822
04:31:10,650 --> 04:31:15,110
I was trying to refresh the stupid video, and boom, I'm upside down and there's smoke everywhere.

4823
04:31:15,450 --> 04:31:17,830
I think Booty Bang owes everyone a big apology.

4824
04:31:18,370 --> 04:31:19,530
Come on, guys, do better.

4825
04:31:20,250 --> 04:31:21,170
And you know what?

4826
04:31:21,450 --> 04:31:24,650
He probably even got a raise after that.

4827
04:31:29,170 --> 04:31:29,730
Yeah.

4828
04:31:29,730 --> 04:31:31,430
Alright, let's actually go to bed.

4829
04:31:32,310 --> 04:31:33,650
It's six in the morning.

4830
04:31:34,910 --> 04:31:36,510
Sleep until noon.

4831
04:31:38,410 --> 04:31:39,370
That sounds right.

4832
04:31:47,800 --> 04:31:48,460
Get dressed.

4833
04:31:49,020 --> 04:31:50,420
What happens if I click that?

4834
04:31:50,580 --> 04:31:51,800
Okay, I should immediately get dressed.

4835
04:31:51,980 --> 04:31:52,040
Okay.

4836
04:31:53,040 --> 04:31:53,300
Sweet.

4837
04:31:54,140 --> 04:31:55,520
I guess we skipped the shower today.

4838
04:31:55,700 --> 04:31:56,000
You know what?

4839
04:31:56,120 --> 04:31:57,120
That's actually a good idea.

4840
04:31:58,260 --> 04:31:59,360
Workout window opens.

4841
04:31:59,760 --> 04:32:01,420
We're gonna get a workout a different way today.

4842
04:32:03,240 --> 04:32:04,860
I don't know how often you should feed a snake.

4843
04:32:05,000 --> 04:32:07,820
I guess tonight I'll feed that snake again.

4844
04:32:08,620 --> 04:32:09,620
Let's go do some painting.

4845
04:32:13,710 --> 04:32:15,550
Some chores around the house.

4846
04:32:16,870 --> 04:32:20,690
Stormy blue paint or tropical green paint?

4847
04:32:21,770 --> 04:32:22,350
Hmm.

4848
04:32:23,830 --> 04:32:24,530
Stormy.

4849
04:32:26,230 --> 04:32:26,990
Definitely.

4850
04:32:36,770 --> 04:32:37,530
Yes.

4851
04:32:38,290 --> 04:32:39,210
Come on, Jason.

4852
04:32:39,750 --> 04:32:40,750
Oh, I gotta do it.

4853
04:32:40,830 --> 04:32:41,150
Okay, okay.

4854
04:32:41,350 --> 04:32:41,730
I'm down.

4855
04:32:49,140 --> 04:32:49,660
Nice.

4856
04:32:49,660 --> 04:32:50,940
Ooh, I love that sound.

4857
04:32:53,260 --> 04:32:53,780
Yes.

4858
04:32:56,260 --> 04:32:57,700
GTA 6, people.

4859
04:32:59,780 --> 04:33:00,760
And I love it.

4860
04:33:07,700 --> 04:33:08,940
This guy is brave, though.

4861
04:33:10,080 --> 04:33:11,880
No protection at all on the floor.

4862
04:33:15,610 --> 04:33:16,630
I guess he's just confident.

4863
04:33:19,970 --> 04:33:20,970
What about the roof, though?

4864
04:33:21,110 --> 04:33:22,750
Like, why did you leave such a gap down there?

4865
04:33:26,490 --> 04:33:27,870
Okay, he's kind of doing it, I guess.

4866
04:33:29,930 --> 04:33:31,670
Okay, how are you going to handle that outlet, though?

4867
04:33:31,890 --> 04:33:32,650
Let me see the skills.

4868
04:33:33,830 --> 04:33:35,390
You got to put some tape around that, brother.

4869
04:33:40,330 --> 04:33:41,190
Oh, here it goes.

4870
04:33:41,310 --> 04:33:44,330
Is he gonna... Oh, they don't even show that.

4871
04:33:45,550 --> 04:33:46,770
I needed to see his technique.

4872
04:33:47,030 --> 04:33:48,270
Okay, wait a minute.

4873
04:33:48,410 --> 04:33:49,770
This is not the blue I was imagining.

4874
04:33:51,590 --> 04:33:52,710
That's more like turquoise.

4875
04:33:55,090 --> 04:33:56,230
That's right, I know my colors.

4876
04:34:00,060 --> 04:34:01,420
I gotta figure out how to fish.

4877
04:34:02,020 --> 04:34:05,300
But maybe we should... Oh, wait a minute.

4878
04:34:05,560 --> 04:34:06,780
We need to fix the roof as well.

4879
04:34:08,220 --> 04:34:09,100
We ain't done here.

4880
04:34:10,380 --> 04:34:10,780
Whoa!

4881
04:34:16,320 --> 04:34:17,160
There's a bird up there.

4882
04:34:19,380 --> 04:34:19,780
Inspect?

4883
04:34:25,480 --> 04:34:25,920
What?

4884
04:34:27,820 --> 04:34:28,260
Oh.

4885
04:34:29,120 --> 04:34:31,180
Wait, you can actually just zoom in on things?

4886
04:34:34,340 --> 04:34:35,560
Or was that... No?

4887
04:34:35,900 --> 04:34:39,100
When I stand like this, I can... Oh, it's this button.

4888
04:34:39,840 --> 04:34:41,160
Oh, that's so nice!

4889
04:34:41,540 --> 04:34:42,640
I have to remember this.

4890
04:34:43,600 --> 04:34:47,200
You can go into a sort of semi-first-person mode there.

4891
04:34:47,580 --> 04:34:48,520
Just to look around.

4892
04:34:48,660 --> 04:34:49,040
That's neat.

4893
04:34:55,300 --> 04:34:56,080
All right, Jason.

4894
04:34:58,100 --> 04:34:59,320
Are we done with the roof here?

4895
04:35:01,500 --> 04:35:02,720
We were done with the roof.

4896
04:35:03,040 --> 04:35:03,560
Let me see what it said.

4897
04:35:08,040 --> 04:35:09,740
Oh, railing and steps.

4898
04:35:11,040 --> 04:35:14,060
Railing is the thing on the landing here, isn't it?

4899
04:35:16,580 --> 04:35:18,240
I guess we've got to find the spot that's broken.

4900
04:35:23,700 --> 04:35:24,680
And we're back here.

4901
04:35:34,500 --> 04:35:36,280
Do we see a railing that's broken?

4902
04:35:39,920 --> 04:35:40,660
What is that?

4903
04:35:46,210 --> 04:35:47,090
Is that a brick?

4904
04:35:47,250 --> 04:35:47,910
Oh, wait a minute.

4905
04:35:47,990 --> 04:35:51,730
It's the thing that you use to smoothen the edges on wood.

4906
04:35:54,210 --> 04:35:55,030
Oh, here we go.

4907
04:36:00,290 --> 04:36:01,150
There it is.

4908
04:36:02,950 --> 04:36:04,890
Yeah, it just has that line next to him.

4909
04:36:05,610 --> 04:36:06,330
Ready to go.

4910
04:36:16,570 --> 04:36:19,750
Like, I wouldn't mind a whole game just with this, you know?

4911
04:36:19,870 --> 04:36:20,470
Home restoration.

4912
04:36:21,630 --> 04:36:22,610
Sign me up, man.

4913
04:36:24,470 --> 04:36:26,050
I don't care about shooting people.

4914
04:36:26,310 --> 04:36:27,350
Let me fix my home.

4915
04:36:31,510 --> 04:36:32,510
Okay, so that's done.

4916
04:36:32,890 --> 04:36:33,330
Wonderful.

4917
04:36:39,160 --> 04:36:42,440
And the last one, I think, is actually back here.

4918
04:36:44,940 --> 04:36:46,600
So much character to this home.

4919
04:36:47,500 --> 04:36:48,160
Isn't there?

4920
04:36:50,160 --> 04:36:51,900
I want a place like this so bad.

4921
04:36:53,680 --> 04:36:54,880
I think we're just down here.

4922
04:36:55,180 --> 04:36:55,840
Fix the steps.

4923
04:36:58,620 --> 04:36:59,580
Ah, here we go.

4924
04:37:07,270 --> 04:37:10,450
Oh wait, they're old and need replacing maybe.

4925
04:37:12,390 --> 04:37:13,110
Come on.

4926
04:37:13,450 --> 04:37:14,250
There we go.

4927
04:37:16,110 --> 04:37:18,390
All that workout is paying off here.

4928
04:37:24,910 --> 04:37:25,470
Sweet.

4929
04:37:28,550 --> 04:37:32,210
I love that they put so much emphasis on these little things here.

4930
04:37:33,610 --> 04:37:36,550
That actually is very promising for the rest of the game for me.

4931
04:37:38,610 --> 04:37:40,670
This is exactly my type of jam, you know?

4932
04:37:46,950 --> 04:37:47,470
Wonderful.

4933
04:37:53,130 --> 04:37:56,030
The last one.

4934
04:38:01,560 --> 04:38:03,020
I'm a pro with this thing now.

4935
04:38:07,940 --> 04:38:08,380
Yeah.

4936
04:38:10,340 --> 04:38:10,780
Alright.

4937
04:38:11,880 --> 04:38:13,200
House repairs complete.

4938
04:38:15,280 --> 04:38:16,120
That feels good.

4939
04:38:20,920 --> 04:38:21,840
Let's get in the car.

4940
04:38:22,020 --> 04:38:23,260
Hey, let's see if my bike is here.

4941
04:38:23,860 --> 04:38:25,140
Did it actually return?

4942
04:38:25,680 --> 04:38:26,840
It did return.

4943
04:38:27,060 --> 04:38:27,320
Okay.

4944
04:38:27,640 --> 04:38:29,560
So we don't have to worry about picking the bike up.

4945
04:38:33,760 --> 04:38:34,340
Let's go.

4946
04:38:36,500 --> 04:38:36,940
Now.

4947
04:38:38,580 --> 04:38:39,460
Where are we going?

4948
04:38:41,520 --> 04:38:42,960
Why is there a marker right there?

4949
04:38:44,460 --> 04:38:45,100
Remove that.

4950
04:38:46,660 --> 04:38:49,380
I think next up we should do maybe that one.

4951
04:38:50,080 --> 04:38:51,160
Collect Brian's rent.

4952
04:38:51,300 --> 04:38:52,880
It's been a while since we got this mission.

4953
04:38:54,780 --> 04:38:55,740
Let's get down there.

4954
04:38:59,690 --> 04:39:04,650
There's also this weird thing in the shop with the birds that we could check out.

4955
04:39:08,275 --> 04:39:10,542
Arugula, hush!

4956
04:39:11,275 --> 04:39:15,275
Oh my God, Shirley! She is really getting out of control.

4957
04:39:15,275 --> 04:39:17,208
Arugula, shut it!

4958
04:39:17,375 --> 04:39:18,775
Mommy's talking.

4959
04:39:18,908 --> 04:39:23,025
You gotta admit, she has always been more aggressive than the average dog.

4960
04:39:23,358 --> 04:39:28,192
I will not admit that, Peggy! She's just vocal...

4961
04:39:28,458 --> 04:39:30,425
and very, very complicated.

4962
04:39:30,592 --> 04:39:34,225
Well, if you ask me, she needs to be socialized.

4963
04:39:34,358 --> 04:39:35,892
I'll be honest with you, Peggy.

4964
04:39:36,275 --> 04:39:40,242
You are the one who needs to be socialized these days.

4965
04:39:40,508 --> 04:39:42,075
Ever since you got that scooter,

4966
04:39:42,860 --> 04:39:45,760
Ha ha ha.

4967
04:39:45,842 --> 04:39:50,575
I'm not surprised that you're intimidated by a bright little star like Arugula.

4968
04:39:50,575 --> 04:39:54,892
Arugula. You know what, Shirley? At least I leave the house.

4969
04:39:55,892 --> 04:40:00,192
I'd leave too if I got wheeled around everywhere!

4970
04:40:01,900 --> 04:40:05,260
I have never seen anyone in real life on a scooter like that.

4971
04:40:05,740 --> 04:40:06,120
Never.

4972
04:40:07,540 --> 04:40:11,280
I don't even know if that's a real thing in America and people actually do that.

4973
04:40:11,420 --> 04:40:12,640
It seems crazy to me.

4974
04:40:14,320 --> 04:40:15,960
Like, what the fuck, man.

4975
04:40:21,460 --> 04:40:22,180
Alright, let's go.

4976
04:40:27,040 --> 04:40:27,660
Turn right.

4977
04:40:27,720 --> 04:40:29,580
I love that little indicator down there, man.

4978
04:40:33,510 --> 04:40:36,470
In fact, you could probably do without the minimap and just have that indicator.

4979
04:40:38,290 --> 04:40:40,470
Maybe you can actually do that if you turn off minimap.

4980
04:40:41,910 --> 04:40:44,010
I think I'll experiment with that at some point.

4981
04:40:44,970 --> 04:40:47,090
For now, though, I'm just learning the game.

4982
04:40:49,820 --> 04:40:50,720
Getting the basics.

4983
04:40:52,320 --> 04:40:56,440
God, it's funny how everything looks so different depending on the time of day.

4984
04:40:56,780 --> 04:40:59,640
This is almost not recognizable right now for me.

4985
04:41:00,880 --> 04:41:03,520
Because I've mostly been driving here at night and stuff, in dusk.

4986
04:41:10,160 --> 04:41:12,700
That looks like a money transport thingy.

4987
04:41:12,700 --> 04:41:16,840
I wonder if that's a thing in this game where you can rob vehicles like that.

4988
04:41:20,320 --> 04:41:20,980
That'd be dope.

4989
04:41:21,640 --> 04:41:23,220
Also, I need to take care of this car here.

4990
04:41:23,360 --> 04:41:25,920
It's looking hella clean right now, doesn't it?

4991
04:41:26,680 --> 04:41:27,820
We can't mess this up.

4992
04:41:31,500 --> 04:41:32,460
It's very important.

4993
04:41:34,960 --> 04:41:37,840
Okay, so we have to retrieve some money here for Brian.

4994
04:41:43,540 --> 04:41:44,560
People having arguments?

4995
04:41:55,470 --> 04:41:56,130
Wait a minute.

4996
04:41:56,470 --> 04:41:58,290
This GPS is leading me astray.

4997
04:42:00,370 --> 04:42:01,250
It's right here.

4998
04:42:05,830 --> 04:42:07,410
Man, look at the driving skills.

4999
04:42:11,110 --> 04:42:11,890
Oh, shit!

5000
04:42:15,950 --> 04:42:16,710
My bad.

5001
04:42:17,010 --> 04:42:17,290
Sorry.

5002
04:42:17,970 --> 04:42:18,730
Oh, no.

5003
04:42:18,850 --> 04:42:20,110
Look at the scratches, man.

5004
04:42:20,190 --> 04:42:21,490
I just had it repaired.

5005
04:42:22,630 --> 04:42:23,130
Fuck.

5006
04:42:28,680 --> 04:42:29,260
Damn.

5007
04:42:29,260 --> 04:42:30,320
Yeah, yeah.

5008
04:42:31,200 --> 04:42:32,060
Shut up.

5009
04:42:33,580 --> 04:42:34,880
Alright, let's go back here.

5010
04:42:37,160 --> 04:42:38,660
Why does this look like a kindergarten?

5011
04:42:48,180 --> 04:42:49,920
I keep getting different stories out of people.

5012
04:42:50,220 --> 04:42:55,920
One guy says the Majestic is... So you just listen to everyone's conversations, or...?

5013
04:42:55,920 --> 04:42:56,800
Would you relax?

5014
04:42:57,220 --> 04:42:59,200
Why the hell have you got it in for me?

5015
04:42:59,880 --> 04:43:00,840
Come over here and help me out!

5016
04:43:00,840 --> 04:43:01,620
Frank, where are you going?

5017
04:43:04,770 --> 04:43:05,950
The fuck's your problem?

5018
04:43:16,690 --> 04:43:22,970
What the fuck is this guy's problem?

5019
04:43:23,170 --> 04:43:24,030
What did I do to him?

5020
04:43:24,890 --> 04:43:26,870
I'm trying not to start shit here, you know?

5021
04:43:27,870 --> 04:43:29,890
I'm trying to keep it on the lowdown here.

5022
04:43:36,200 --> 04:43:38,460
Dude, I am so close to knocking this guy out.

5023
04:43:40,400 --> 04:43:40,880
What?

5024
04:43:52,640 --> 04:44:00,720
Sorry, I was just, you know... He was talking about eating something out of a stripper's ass and it would cost him 60k.

5025
04:44:02,860 --> 04:44:03,340
Cool.

5026
04:44:07,280 --> 04:44:08,720
Moonshine Boutique.

5027
04:44:13,640 --> 04:44:15,480
Wait, what am I supposed to do with contacts here?

5028
04:44:16,740 --> 04:44:18,340
Oh wait, Shirley sent us a message.

5029
04:44:19,880 --> 04:44:20,940
Thanks Han, my Ramos.

5030
04:44:21,220 --> 04:44:22,360
Oh yeah, we already did that one.

5031
04:44:23,700 --> 04:44:24,100
Done.

5032
04:44:26,640 --> 04:44:27,320
Reminders, maybe.

5033
04:44:28,840 --> 04:44:30,300
No, she posted again.

5034
04:44:32,420 --> 04:44:33,860
Oh, select contacts, I'm blind.

5035
04:44:36,840 --> 04:44:37,700
Let's see what he wants.

5036
04:44:38,780 --> 04:44:40,060
He's gonna give us some info on this.

5037
04:44:46,360 --> 04:44:48,320
Hey, so I'm at that boutique.

5038
04:44:48,460 --> 04:44:49,500
Yeah, boutique.

5039
04:44:49,720 --> 04:44:53,340
Ask those dorks how many wind chimes they sold since they moved in there.

5040
04:44:53,560 --> 04:44:54,580
It's an acid lab.

5041
04:44:54,800 --> 04:44:55,120
Okay.

5042
04:44:55,600 --> 04:44:56,840
So how do you want me to play this?

5043
04:44:57,000 --> 04:44:58,160
However you like.

5044
04:44:58,180 --> 04:45:01,100
I want my cut, and I want them out of there.

5045
04:45:01,340 --> 04:45:02,940
I covered them for long enough.

5046
04:45:05,040 --> 04:45:06,620
It's an acid lab?

5047
04:45:08,480 --> 04:45:11,140
To be honest, though, this whole place reminds me of Christiania.

5048
04:45:11,960 --> 04:45:15,340
A part of Copenhagen that is, like, a little self-sustaining.

5049
04:45:16,400 --> 04:45:19,760
And let's just say free in their ways.

5050
04:45:22,180 --> 04:45:23,120
Lab fees.

5051
04:45:23,275 --> 04:45:25,242
Welcome, welcome...

5052
04:45:25,520 --> 04:45:26,500
What's going on?

5053
04:45:27,275 --> 04:45:30,342
Hey, how ya doin'? Brian sent me over here for the rent.

5054
04:45:30,575 --> 04:45:33,108
Yeah. Don't have it, dude.

5055
04:45:37,558 --> 04:45:38,958
[sighs] I don't know, dude.

5056
04:45:39,025 --> 04:45:41,325
I didn't make any money this month, or...

5057
04:45:41,558 --> 04:45:43,392
someone stole it from me. Make it up.

5058
04:45:43,480 --> 04:45:46,420
It's just a bullshit social construct anyways, my guy.

5059
04:45:46,620 --> 04:45:48,740
Point is, fuck Brian.

5060
04:45:48,980 --> 04:45:50,660
He ain't putting in the work like moi.

5061
04:45:52,420 --> 04:45:52,900
Huh.

5062
04:45:56,820 --> 04:45:58,280
Let's do this the easy way, bro.

5063
04:45:58,660 --> 04:46:00,160
Just give me Brian's rent and I'm gone.

5064
04:46:00,600 --> 04:46:01,780
Look, just think about it.

5065
04:46:01,860 --> 04:46:03,160
Does Brian really need the money?

5066
04:46:03,400 --> 04:46:04,160
Forget him.

5067
04:46:04,500 --> 04:46:05,600
That's how you wanna do it?

5068
04:46:06,160 --> 04:46:07,120
Yeah, I do.

5069
04:46:08,000 --> 04:46:09,340
Do something about it.

5070
04:46:12,592 --> 04:46:13,658
Ahh, no!

5071
04:46:14,380 --> 04:46:15,800
Whoa, hey!

5072
04:46:18,392 --> 04:46:20,592
Playtime's over, moron. Settle up.

5073
04:46:21,275 --> 04:46:22,125
The rent. Now.

5074
04:46:22,692 --> 04:46:24,142
Stop, stop! Okay!

5075
04:46:24,375 --> 04:46:27,508
I don't have the rent. Just- just take the acid.

5076
04:46:27,542 --> 04:46:34,475
It's in the backroom! The code is 0420.. Ugh...

5077
04:46:34,542 --> 04:46:36,208
Like, right now? What about...

5078
04:46:36,808 --> 04:46:38,008
Yup, you got it!

5079
04:46:40,590 --> 04:46:41,750
0420, of course.

5080
04:46:44,070 --> 04:46:44,670
Dude...

5081
04:46:45,400 --> 04:46:47,220
I wish I could smash up his shop.

5082
04:46:48,200 --> 04:46:49,200
That's what I would do.

5083
04:46:49,680 --> 04:46:50,120
Restrained.

5084
04:46:51,880 --> 04:46:54,140
Wait, so these actions I have here actually do matter.

5085
04:46:55,420 --> 04:46:56,700
Look at all the detail.

5086
04:46:56,860 --> 04:46:58,060
How are they doing this?

5087
04:46:59,180 --> 04:47:00,280
This looks unreal.

5088
04:47:04,580 --> 04:47:05,020
Wow.

5089
04:47:06,300 --> 04:47:07,400
Let me see if I can actually...

5090
04:47:11,850 --> 04:47:12,470
Jason!

5091
04:47:13,650 --> 04:47:14,730
Are you stupid?

5092
04:47:16,530 --> 04:47:17,710
Toggle arc on?

5093
04:47:20,330 --> 04:47:21,230
Wait, arc?

5094
04:47:22,850 --> 04:47:24,370
Oh, for throwing, I guess.

5095
04:47:27,950 --> 04:47:28,390
Okay.

5096
04:47:29,010 --> 04:47:29,650
Just testing.

5097
04:47:31,490 --> 04:47:32,830
Alright, let's get back there.

5098
04:47:34,050 --> 04:47:35,110
Let's collect that shit.

5099
04:47:35,830 --> 04:47:36,630
0420, was it?

5100
04:47:38,390 --> 04:47:38,970
What's that?

5101
04:47:40,390 --> 04:47:44,310
List, glass beakers, burners, chips, tie-dye shirts, new bong.

5102
04:47:47,650 --> 04:47:48,090
0420.

5103
04:47:49,230 --> 04:47:52,270
Wait, so if I hadn't gotten the code from him, I could have gotten it here.

5104
04:47:54,810 --> 04:47:55,470
That's cool.

5105
04:48:02,880 --> 04:48:04,780
Kinda shitty security, I'll have to say.

5106
04:48:14,220 --> 04:48:14,720
Nice.

5107
04:48:16,180 --> 04:48:19,700
Am I gonna expect some company here, or...

5108
04:48:20,558 --> 04:48:21,858
Ah. Here we go.

5109
04:48:24,450 --> 04:48:24,950
Okay.

5110
04:48:25,530 --> 04:48:27,310
That looks sophisticated.

5111
04:48:29,930 --> 04:48:34,070
Stow bags and items in any vehicle trunk, including your personal vehicle, for easy transport.

5112
04:48:36,790 --> 04:48:37,290
Aha.

5113
04:48:43,190 --> 04:48:44,690
Oh, I just broke that like that.

5114
04:48:44,690 --> 04:48:44,950
Okay.

5115
04:48:51,080 --> 04:48:52,040
That's a lot of drugs.

5116
04:48:53,680 --> 04:48:55,660
I wonder if I can take the drugs and use them.

5117
04:48:56,300 --> 04:48:56,920
Probably not.

5118
04:48:59,380 --> 04:49:00,900
I mean, it is a GTA game.

5119
04:49:01,600 --> 04:49:02,260
Who knows.

5120
04:49:04,120 --> 04:49:04,560
Okay.

5121
04:49:05,120 --> 04:49:06,260
We got the good stuff.

5122
04:49:08,220 --> 04:49:09,080
Let's get out of here.

5123
04:49:11,740 --> 04:49:12,180
Brian!

5124
04:49:13,120 --> 04:49:14,100
I got your shit.

5125
04:49:25,030 --> 04:49:28,990
Well, he didn't have enough cash for his rent, but... I got some acid, though.

5126
04:49:29,650 --> 04:49:30,410
Will I cover your cut?

5127
04:49:30,630 --> 04:49:31,650
It'll do for now.

5128
04:49:32,090 --> 04:49:35,910
I gotta lock up next door at the Isla Tropicale private club.

5129
04:49:36,350 --> 04:49:39,290
Head inside, put whatever you got in the strong box.

5130
04:49:39,290 --> 04:49:41,730
I'll swing by later to see if we're square.

5131
04:49:42,030 --> 04:49:42,330
Cool.

5132
04:49:42,790 --> 04:49:43,750
Do I need a key or something?

5133
04:49:43,890 --> 04:49:44,630
Oh, right.

5134
04:49:44,630 --> 04:49:46,290
I forgot this was a Donnie job.

5135
04:49:46,570 --> 04:49:50,010
The code is 7700.

5136
04:49:50,790 --> 04:49:51,350
Got it.

5137
04:49:55,180 --> 04:49:55,700
Okay.

5138
04:49:55,700 --> 04:49:57,120
View nearby locations.

5139
04:49:58,040 --> 04:50:00,460
Select Brian's lockup?

5140
04:50:03,980 --> 04:50:04,500
Oh!

5141
04:50:05,860 --> 04:50:06,860
Oh, that's cool.

5142
04:50:07,320 --> 04:50:08,900
That's like a quick way to do it.

5143
04:50:09,540 --> 04:50:13,560
Brian will pay for any narcotics, jewelry, and marked bills dropped off at his lockup.

5144
04:50:20,340 --> 04:50:20,700
Done.

5145
04:50:20,700 --> 04:50:21,060
Okay.

5146
04:50:21,700 --> 04:50:23,040
I just want to take a look in here though.

5147
04:50:27,900 --> 04:50:30,800
Maybe I shouldn't be walking around with a bat in my hand.

5148
04:50:31,980 --> 04:50:33,120
Can I like stow that?

5149
04:50:40,390 --> 04:50:41,870
I guess I don't need to carry that around.

5150
04:50:42,570 --> 04:50:43,670
I don't want to scare her.

5151
04:50:45,030 --> 04:50:45,410
Hey!

5152
04:50:51,730 --> 04:50:53,850
Let me have a look around.

5153
04:50:56,330 --> 04:50:57,910
Now I know I can zoom in.

5154
04:51:01,260 --> 04:51:02,260
Wait, how does that work again?

5155
04:51:03,620 --> 04:51:05,220
No, don't, don't do that.

5156
04:51:05,920 --> 04:51:07,400
Yeah, sorry, I was trying to zoom.

5157
04:51:07,940 --> 04:51:08,620
You know how it is.

5158
04:51:08,840 --> 04:51:10,420
And then you accidentally pull out a gat.

5159
04:51:11,920 --> 04:51:12,540
Changing room.

5160
04:51:15,970 --> 04:51:18,430
I guess you can walk in here if you have cops on you.

5161
04:51:19,130 --> 04:51:22,210
Quickly change out the drip.

5162
04:51:24,350 --> 04:51:26,250
So wait, how do I actually zoom on command?

5163
04:51:26,830 --> 04:51:27,790
I need to figure this out.

5164
04:51:27,930 --> 04:51:29,170
So I hold this button.

5165
04:51:30,090 --> 04:51:36,790
Then I wait for an interaction prompt or... Do not pull the gun out, Jason.

5166
04:51:38,150 --> 04:51:39,390
I know you were in the army.

5167
04:51:39,630 --> 04:51:41,810
You don't have to, you know, tell everybody all the time.

5168
04:51:42,450 --> 04:51:42,870
Bracelets.

5169
04:51:45,040 --> 04:51:47,180
No way I get to wear bracelets too.

5170
04:51:48,280 --> 04:51:49,360
I mean, why not?

5171
04:51:50,540 --> 04:51:54,960
We can... I like that one.

5172
04:52:00,940 --> 04:52:01,460
Yep.

5173
04:52:01,460 --> 04:52:01,980
Thanks.

5174
04:52:03,040 --> 04:52:03,820
It's cool.

5175
04:52:05,080 --> 04:52:05,740
T-shirts.

5176
04:52:05,900 --> 04:52:06,260
What's this?

5177
04:52:07,940 --> 04:52:09,480
Bonbon tanning oil.

5178
04:52:09,760 --> 04:52:10,540
What even is that?

5179
04:52:10,820 --> 04:52:13,720
You put it on and you... Oh, wait.

5180
04:52:13,780 --> 04:52:14,860
It's like the fake tan.

5181
04:52:15,040 --> 04:52:16,100
You spray your tan on.

5182
04:52:16,480 --> 04:52:17,300
Never understood that.

5183
04:52:21,660 --> 04:52:26,600
I mean, that's just... I guess if you go swimming...

5184
04:52:29,520 --> 04:52:30,640
What's happening out there?

5185
04:52:32,880 --> 04:52:34,400
Flat-top aviators.

5186
04:52:37,120 --> 04:52:38,080
29 bucks.

5187
04:52:38,780 --> 04:52:39,460
You know what?

5188
04:52:39,580 --> 04:52:40,320
I'll take him.

5189
04:52:42,420 --> 04:52:43,840
That's Vice City right there.

5190
04:52:45,760 --> 04:52:46,900
Something about it, you know?

5191
04:52:47,560 --> 04:52:48,060
Thank you!

5192
04:53:08,500 --> 04:53:09,140
The potluck?

5193
04:53:11,100 --> 04:53:13,480
Ooh, I really want to steal this scooter.

5194
04:53:15,220 --> 04:53:17,780
Actually, I want to take it and put it in the trunk of my car.

5195
04:53:19,400 --> 04:53:20,700
I doubt I can do it, though.

5196
04:53:21,450 --> 04:53:22,650
But I would love to do it.

5197
04:53:23,390 --> 04:53:24,630
I can't leave my car behind.

5198
04:53:30,430 --> 04:53:32,830
Okay, so he puts the... in his car.

5199
04:53:39,610 --> 04:53:41,210
Did one of my lights go out in the back?

5200
04:53:42,590 --> 04:53:44,510
I think I broke one of my lights.

5201
04:53:46,430 --> 04:53:49,990
Yeah, look, the blinker is on in the front, but the backlight isn't working.

5202
04:53:52,130 --> 04:53:53,070
This side is working.

5203
04:53:54,890 --> 04:53:55,850
Dude, I love that.

5204
04:53:56,370 --> 04:53:57,110
Great detail.

5205
04:53:57,270 --> 04:53:58,510
We gotta get this shit repaired again.

5206
04:54:04,270 --> 04:54:07,690
Okay, let's just go straight there and drop off this thing, this asset.

5207
04:54:28,860 --> 04:54:30,140
That's the place right there.

5208
04:54:37,120 --> 04:54:37,680
Okay!

5209
04:54:39,880 --> 04:54:40,660
Sound good?

5210
04:54:45,620 --> 04:54:47,560
Dude, I'm drinking in these environments.

5211
04:54:48,060 --> 04:54:52,580
Like, everywhere I drive, I'm just, like, soaking it, you know, like a sponge.

5212
04:54:53,520 --> 04:54:56,760
And a bunch of good chemicals are being released in my brain.

5213
04:54:57,000 --> 04:54:57,660
Every time.

5214
04:54:59,460 --> 04:55:01,180
Graphics matter, if you do it right.

5215
04:55:02,940 --> 04:55:11,500
Obviously, gameplay is king, but you can't deny that in a game that's trying to simulate real life to an extent, graphics are important.

5216
04:55:12,260 --> 04:55:12,900
You know?

5217
04:55:14,890 --> 04:55:16,270
I fucking nailed it.

5218
04:55:19,570 --> 04:55:24,590
I need the bag and Brian Strongbox for him to collect later.

5219
04:55:25,470 --> 04:55:25,930
Sure.

5220
04:55:31,870 --> 04:55:32,690
Oh yeah.

5221
04:55:37,710 --> 04:55:39,630
Drop that stuff from the boutique.

5222
04:55:44,440 --> 04:55:49,480
I don't know if I'm a fan of that music, that little song that plays after a mission.

5223
04:55:50,480 --> 04:55:54,760
It's not quite iconic the same way, you know, San Andreas' music was, for example.

5224
04:55:55,820 --> 04:55:56,300
Thanks, son.

5225
04:55:56,560 --> 04:55:57,600
I'll check them when I can.

5226
04:55:57,740 --> 04:55:59,300
Got other business to take care of first.

5227
04:56:00,320 --> 04:56:01,220
Sounds good, Brian.

5228
04:56:02,800 --> 04:56:04,300
Got engines for boats here.

5229
04:56:04,960 --> 04:56:06,400
Bring stolen goods to drop-offs.

5230
04:56:06,500 --> 04:56:08,740
Like Brian's lock-up, you'll get paid after they're collected.

5231
04:56:09,740 --> 04:56:12,800
So wait, I can just, like, go around and steal stuff or what?

5232
04:56:15,350 --> 04:56:16,430
Hold on, let me sue him.

5233
04:56:16,950 --> 04:56:18,270
Oh, now I can inspect.

5234
04:56:18,610 --> 04:56:19,870
Maybe it's only indoors.

5235
04:56:23,590 --> 04:56:24,690
That's a nice poster.

5236
04:56:25,070 --> 04:56:26,330
That is very American.

5237
04:56:26,930 --> 04:56:29,770
She's got the American flag on her... boops.

5238
04:56:32,690 --> 04:56:34,710
Is she out there doing archery?

5239
04:56:34,870 --> 04:56:35,890
Bow hunting, maybe.

5240
04:56:41,430 --> 04:56:43,330
Also, I think I messed up the keybind.

5241
04:56:43,410 --> 04:56:45,390
Maybe you can zoom outside.

5242
04:56:46,290 --> 04:56:48,150
I forgot to click R3.

5243
04:56:48,410 --> 04:56:49,970
Instead, I tried to press R2.

5244
04:56:54,610 --> 04:56:55,810
Is that... hold on, is that weed?

5245
04:56:59,430 --> 04:57:00,830
Can I grab one of these real quick?

5246
04:57:01,210 --> 04:57:02,770
I see some of them are rolled already.

5247
04:57:06,260 --> 04:57:07,080
Probably wouldn't mind.

5248
04:57:07,900 --> 04:57:09,040
Okay, I can't click on that.

5249
04:57:09,840 --> 04:57:10,720
Alright, let's get out of here.

5250
04:57:11,760 --> 04:57:12,300
That's nice.

5251
04:57:27,010 --> 04:57:28,250
What are they doing over there?

5252
04:57:29,130 --> 04:57:29,930
Having a beer.

5253
04:57:30,370 --> 04:57:31,090
Should we go join them?

5254
04:57:32,890 --> 04:57:33,730
Let's go join them.

5255
04:57:35,910 --> 04:57:40,770
Just go over there and be like, hey, so I noticed in my binoculars that you guys were having a party.

5256
04:57:41,770 --> 04:57:43,110
And I had to join in.

5257
04:57:44,130 --> 04:57:47,610
That's such a creepy thing to say if you approach someone like that.

5258
04:57:49,790 --> 04:57:50,190
Hey!

5259
04:58:06,180 --> 04:58:06,700
Ha!

5260
04:58:06,960 --> 04:58:06,960
Ha!

5261
04:58:09,890 --> 04:58:10,710
What was that?

5262
04:58:19,830 --> 04:58:20,530
See ya.

5263
04:58:21,710 --> 04:58:22,250
Noops.

5264
04:58:23,930 --> 04:58:25,490
Are they actually following me?

5265
04:58:30,810 --> 04:58:32,330
They went back to their thing.

5266
04:58:33,950 --> 04:58:35,070
I'm a menace.

5267
04:58:47,590 --> 04:58:48,490
Oh shit!

5268
04:58:55,810 --> 04:58:56,710
Hey, Brian!

5269
04:58:57,590 --> 04:58:58,150
Jason!

5270
04:58:58,450 --> 04:58:58,850
What's up?

5271
04:58:59,270 --> 04:58:59,950
I need you.

5272
04:59:00,230 --> 04:59:02,250
I'm meeting Arnold, my contact.

5273
04:59:05,808 --> 04:59:08,608
the guy who brokered that Kingfisher deal.

5274
04:59:08,875 --> 04:59:11,325
I'd like to make sure we're all hunky dory

5275
04:59:11,358 --> 04:59:14,092
after whatever you boys did the other day.

5276
04:59:14,092 --> 04:59:15,625
Sure, man. Whatever you need...

5277
04:59:15,858 --> 04:59:19,992
Alright. Now come meet us over at, the Crastenburg pool bar.

5278
04:59:20,025 --> 04:59:23,158
And, you know what, make sure you got a piece.

5279
04:59:23,592 --> 04:59:25,425
I'm not taking any chances.

5280
04:59:27,320 --> 04:59:27,760
Okay.

5281
04:59:27,760 --> 04:59:29,340
I mean, I got a piece.

5282
04:59:30,260 --> 04:59:31,540
In fact, I got a couple.

5283
04:59:33,140 --> 04:59:34,320
Let me see where that is.

5284
04:59:38,020 --> 04:59:38,720
Meet Brian.

5285
04:59:39,300 --> 04:59:41,620
Brian said to meet him at the Krastenberg Hotel.

5286
04:59:41,860 --> 04:59:42,920
Sounds like there's some trouble.

5287
04:59:44,520 --> 04:59:45,140
Sounds good.

5288
04:59:51,080 --> 04:59:52,840
Hold on, can I actually do a wheel spin or whatever?

5289
05:00:04,740 --> 05:00:07,540
I do wonder if I break my wheels if I do that too much.

5290
05:00:13,230 --> 05:00:15,910
Man, I love the AI on the road in this game.

5291
05:00:17,010 --> 05:00:22,930
They're actually behaving like, well, much more realistic drivers compared to other Grand Theft Autos.

5292
05:00:23,310 --> 05:00:24,970
They're not as annoying either, you know?

5293
05:00:26,070 --> 05:00:28,570
They don't randomly stop or do random shit.

5294
05:00:28,730 --> 05:00:29,670
They just drive.

5295
05:00:30,750 --> 05:00:32,810
Do their thing, and what's going on there?

5296
05:00:34,730 --> 05:00:36,030
Hold up, we gotta investigate.

5297
05:00:38,908 --> 05:00:39,908
Hey, hey, hey!

5298
05:00:40,108 --> 05:00:41,475
I don't need your help!

5299
05:00:46,140 --> 05:00:47,580
Can I look through the window?

5300
05:00:48,620 --> 05:00:49,260
Oh shit.

5301
05:00:51,925 --> 05:00:54,392
You can't catch me! Stop! Hey, stop!

5302
05:00:55,140 --> 05:00:56,820
How do I use this in the car?

5303
05:00:57,692 --> 05:01:00,525
I won't go... I won't go anywhere! I won't go anywhere!

5304
05:01:01,800 --> 05:01:04,120
What is wrong with these people in Leonida?

5305
05:01:05,475 --> 05:01:07,142
Here-here I go!

5306
05:01:07,542 --> 05:01:09,542
Fuck it! Stun! Stun!

5307
05:01:13,960 --> 05:01:15,120
He got tasered.

5308
05:01:15,542 --> 05:01:16,475
What is wrong with you?

5309
05:01:27,920 --> 05:01:29,300
Okay, I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

5310
05:01:31,800 --> 05:01:34,320
I'm leaving, I'm leaving.

5311
05:01:37,475 --> 05:01:39,475
Yeah, they're gonna have fun taking this guy's prints...

5312
05:01:39,475 --> 05:01:45,208
Ooh man, can you imagine? Jesus Christ.

5313
05:01:45,908 --> 05:01:47,742
Dispatch, suspect is in custody.

5314
05:01:50,630 --> 05:01:51,670
Craziest people here.

5315
05:01:52,710 --> 05:01:58,210
Maybe that's just what it's like over in the Oneida or... I'm assuming it's like Florida, right?

5316
05:01:58,670 --> 05:01:59,750
Because the Oneida man.

5317
05:02:02,110 --> 05:02:04,210
I wonder how true to life old is this?

5318
05:02:05,610 --> 05:02:07,590
Or if this is completely overdone, you know?

5319
05:02:15,170 --> 05:02:18,730
I can't get over how fucking realistic some of this lighting is.

5320
05:02:19,450 --> 05:02:22,210
Like, I constantly go like, wait a minute, that looks like a real picture.

5321
05:02:23,850 --> 05:02:24,790
From real life.

5322
05:02:33,110 --> 05:02:35,050
I would say my parking is decent.

5323
05:02:36,030 --> 05:02:39,250
You can manage your loadout in your trunk or any ammunition.

5324
05:02:39,510 --> 05:02:41,070
Oh yeah, right, he wanted us to bring a piece.

5325
05:02:43,980 --> 05:02:45,140
Let me see what I got here.

5326
05:02:46,500 --> 05:02:47,740
I mean, I have a pistol.

5327
05:02:47,940 --> 05:02:48,640
That'll be fine, right?

5328
05:02:48,880 --> 05:02:49,420
Let's close this.

